/**

@page page_exahype_multicore Parallelism within a rank

\tableofcontents

A solver family advances its solution with tarch::accelerator::parallelFor
and tarch::accelerator::parallelReduce over the cell and face spans of the
partition. With the host backend these dispatches are OpenMP loops; with a GPU
backend they are device kernels over the pools in device memory.

# Dispatches

A time step is a fixed sequence of dispatches: the finite-volume family runs
the boundary faces, the local level jumps, the local cells, the remote level
jumps, the remote cells, the face projection and the restriction of the level
jumps; the DG families run the predictor or the stages, the level-jump
interpolation, the Riemann problems, the level-jump restriction and the
corrector. The boundary faces, the local level jumps and the local cells and
faces run between `post()` and `wait()` of the halo exchange, so the messages
travel while the rank computes; a regrid prolongs and restricts on the rank
while the migrated cells travel.

# Tasks

peano4::topology::runChunkedTasks spawns tarch::tasking tasks for the host
work of the tree and partition build after a regrid, one task per chunk of
spawn-level blocks. @ref page_tarch_tasking describes the interfaces.

# Choosing the layout

A rank needs enough cells to fill its threads and to hide its halo exchange
behind its local cells. The MPI decomposition rows of the grid report give the
cells per rank and the rank-boundary faces;
@ref page_exahype_performance_optimisation provides solver-specific guidance.

*/
